---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_43",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 43,
  "text": "<p> [[124.1]] <b>37. JAKOB THOMASIUS AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[124.2]] Leipzig, 7. (17.) Januar 1671. [35.50.]</b></p>\n<p> [[124.13]] Non merebantur <i>dialogi physici</i> mei elogium illud, quod iis tribuis. Majore merito\n[[124.14]] provocabit eruditorum plausus vel illud schediasma tuum, de quo scribis, cujusque veluti\n[[124.15]] summam literis tuis complecteris. In quo cum legerem aetherem illum, quem ais cum luce solis\n[[124.16]] circa terram ferri, videbar equidem agnoscere aliquid, si non idem, saltem forsan simile aetheri\n[[124.17]] de quo ago p. 46, 47, <i>physicorum</i>. Qua in re forte decipior, tamdiu tamen hic error me\n[[124.18]] delectabit, donec ipsam voluptatem alia depellat, ubi ex te didicero certiora. Pro carmine, quod\n[[124.19]] mittis, habeo gratias. Nunc disputatio quaedam habenda me praeside de feminarum eruditione\n[[124.20]] prelo tradita est. Eam occasione proxima mittam. </p>\n<p> [[124.21]] Cum jam in manibus ea esset typographi, notitia demum facta mihi est, libelli, cui titulus:\n[[124.22]] <i>Ehren-Preiß des Frauenzimmers</i>, auctore cancellario Fuldensi Schützio, cui personatus quidam\n[[124.23]] Poliandinus respondit, qui et inde libellum suum nominavit: <i>gestürzten Ehrenpreiß.</i> Ea re\n[[124.24]] factum, ut vix duobus verbis tangere licuerit in disputatione nostra hos duos libellos, vocandos\n[[124.25]] alioqui sub accuratiorem censuram. Decrevi tamen de iis aliquid, ut solemus, praefari. Schützium\n[[124.26]] intelligo apostatam esse, unde venit mihi in mentem suspicari, nomen Ignatii, quod cum\n[[125.1]] Wilhelmo praefert, ipsi inditum esse in professione religionis novae. Poliandinum ajunt, nescio\n[[125.2]] quem esse, Johannem Gorgiam, Transylvanum, hominem nescio an religionis nostrae, dissolutae\n[[125.3]] certe vitae, et e patria profugum, cum ancillae patris vitium intulisset. Ejusdem quoque\n[[125.4]] ajunt esse, <i>den Jungferlichen Zeit-Vertreiber</i>, nomine Veriphantoris editum, scriptum impurum.\n[[125.5]] Quae me res movit, ut crederem, feminei sexus dedignationem, qua plenum est scriptum ejus,\n[[125.6]] Schütziano oppositum, non ex alio fonte proficisci, quam quod feminas non aliunde aestimaret,\n[[125.7]] quam ex eo abusu, quo scorta impuri hominis humores foedos matularum instar excipiunt. Sic\n[[125.8]] vicissim impulsum Schützium credebam tenero quodam, sed coniugali in hunc sexum amore, et\n[[125.9]] misericordia versus eas, quae a viris duriter tractantur; nam in ejusmodi viros aculeum subinde\n[[125.10]] emittit; indignatione insuper in eos, qui optimo sexui convicia dicunt: Huc enim referebam\n[[125.11]] historiam de nescio quo nobili incivili, qui ex itinere Gallico nihil aliud retulerat domum, quam\n[[125.12]] in feminas convicia. Narro tibi somnia mea, ut ex te veriora sive de Schützio, sive de Poliandino\n[[125.13]] discam. Tametsi enim non exspectabit ista praefatio mea tuas literas, jucundum tamen\n[[125.14]] erit, hujus ut ita dicam, monomachiae historiam per te cognoscere. Ajunt esse Schützium\n[[125.15]] insigni munere affectum ab imperatrice, cui dedicavit libellum, tolerabilem, nisi Agrippam\n[[125.16]] secutus, quem semel citat, passim describit, altius levasset hunc sexum, quam eum locaverat\n[[125.17]] creator. </p>\n<p> [[125.18]] Est et aliud quiddam, in quo velim opera tua uti. Suntne tibi notae orationes Nicolai\n[[125.19]] Schoenbergii Cardinalis, coram Julio II. Pontifice, habitae, <i>de pugna Christi cum diabolo in\n[[125.20]] deserto</i>, quas <i>Bibliotheca</i> Gesneri memorat. Eas apud nos etiam a. 1511 editas esse didici e\n[[125.21]] postilla Bausthiana in illud Evangelium, sed frustra quaesivi in nostris bibliothecis: magnopere\n[[125.22]] tamen vellem, vel ipsas, vel apographon earum procurare possem ex illa familia maximo\n[[125.23]] cuidam viro. Quaeso, si me potes, adjuva. Bene vale amice optime, et Illustrissimo Boineburgio\n[[125.24]] fausta quaeque a me, in hunc et sequentes annos, quos et tibi felicissimos fluere iubeat Deus,\n[[125.25]] precare. Lips. d. 7 Jan. anni ineuntis, 1671. </p>\n",
  "number": "37.",
  "title": "JAKOB THOMASIUS AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "Leipzig, 7. (17.) Januar 1671. [35.50.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:37. JAKOB THOMASIUS AN LEIBNIZ Leipzig, 7. (17.) Januar 1671. [35.50.] Non merebantur dialogi physici mei elogium illud, quod iis tribuis. Majore merito provocabit eruditorum plausus vel illud schediasma tuum, de quo scribis, cujusque veluti summam literis tuis complecteris. In quo cum legerem aethe...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>